Stop when the game archive is missing, rather than carrying on without it

`Context::InitResourceManager` returns false when the main archive is not there,
and says so with a message box first. Every other caller in libultraship acts on
that return; `GameEngine::GameEngine` discards it, and the engine goes on to
build its window, console and GUI with a resource manager that loaded nothing.

The fault then arrives much later, in game code that assumes the resources are
present. On this platform it is a page fault inside a decompiled function -
`func_800339C4`, called from `func_80033AE0` - reported against libkernel,
because the null reaches it through a libc routine libkernel provides. Nothing
in that report mentions the missing file, which is the whole problem: the title
already knew, ten thousand instructions earlier, and said nothing the player
could act on.

Reporting and stopping there keeps the message the player needs and drops the
crash. `exit` parks the process on this platform, which is a conforming ending
for a big app.

diff --git a/src/port/Engine.cpp b/src/port/Engine.cpp
index 2cd2c99..6f316ea 100644
--- a/src/port/Engine.cpp
+++ b/src/port/Engine.cpp
@@ -167,7 +167,19 @@ GameEngine::GameEngine() {
                   });
     auto controlDeck = std::make_shared<LUS::ControlDeck>(std::vector<CONTROLLERBUTTONS_T>(), defaultMappings, buttonNames);
     const std::string assets_path = Ship::Context::LocateFileAcrossAppDirs(engine_asset_file);
-    this->context->InitResourceManager({assets_path}, {}, 3); // without this line InitWindow fails in Gui::Init()
+    // without this line InitWindow fails in Gui::Init()
+    if (!this->context->InitResourceManager({assets_path}, {}, 3)) {
+        // The archive is not there. libultraship has already said so and returned false,
+        // and every caller but this one acts on it; carrying on leaves the engine with no
+        // resources and the fault arrives later, inside game code that assumes they
+        // loaded - on this platform as a page fault in a decompiled function, with
+        // nothing in the log connecting it to the missing file.
+        GameEngine::ShowMessage("Game data not found",
+                                "mk64.o2r is missing. Convert a Mario Kart 64 ROM to it "
+                                "and copy the archive beside the game.",
+                                SDL_MESSAGEBOX_ERROR);
+        exit(1);
+    }
     this->context->InitConsole(); // without this line the GuiWindow constructor fails in ConsoleWindow::InitElement()
 
     auto gui = std::make_shared<Ship::SpaghettiGui>(std::vector<std::shared_ptr<Ship::GuiWindow>>({}));
